[38;2;124;124;124mThe key idea: We want to show that if a₁ + a₂ ≤ aₙ (sorted), then SR ≥ n² + 1.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mOne approach: Use the fact that for positive reals, we can write SR = n² + Σᵢ<ⱼ [0m[38;2;124;124;124m(aᵢ/aⱼ + aⱼ/aᵢ - 2) = n² + Σᵢ<ⱼ (aᵢ - aⱼ)²/(aᵢ aⱼ).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo SR - n² = Σᵢ<ⱼ (aᵢ - aⱼ)²/(aᵢ aⱼ).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mWe need to show this is ≥ 1 when a₁ + a₂ ≤ aₙ.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo we need: Σᵢ<ⱼ (aᵢ - aⱼ)²/(aᵢ aⱼ) ≥ 1.[0m

